==Trivia==
*Karamja is likely named after the {{wp|Karamoja}} region in Uganda, an equatorial country with a tropical climate not unlike Karamja. In the {{wp|Swahili language}}, spoken in some parts of Uganda, the word ''[[wiktionary:bwana#Swahili|bwana]]'' means "master," "mister," or "boss". Denizens of Karamja use the same word to mean "friend."{{CiteNPC|npc=Trufitus|quote=[What does Bwana mean?] It means friend, and friends come in peace. I assume that you come in peace?|loc=|notes=|name=}}

